From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 13:01:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(control): a settings reload no longer crashes the window

Found by hand, saving a setting with a ghostty pane open, and it took the whole
process with it: an access violation calling BackgroundImage() on a null
IControlAppearance.

TermControl reads the appearance the core hands it without checking -
_UpdateSettingsFromUIThread does `_focused ? FocusedAppearance() :
UnfocusedAppearance()` and dereferences the result - so cascadia's core never
returns null there. It falls back to the settings object and keeps a separate
bool for whether a distinct unfocused appearance was configured. This core
stored the argument as it came, which is null for the great majority of profiles
- so "any profile without an unfocusedAppearance, any settings change, pane not
focused" was a crash. Pre-existing since Phase 5, and nothing had exercised a
settings *reload* on a ghostty pane before today.

Also from the same hand session: search now lands on the match cascadia lands
on. Both engines pick the match nearest the bottom, and ghostty's own first
choice is that one (selectNext with nothing selected takes
active_results[len - 1]), so the control asks for ghostty's rather than
modelling cascadia's idea of "nearest".

Verified against the repro, not just the test: a ghostty pane launched by GUID,
then three settings reloads driven through settings.json - the same path the
Settings UI takes - all survived, where the first crashed before.

The regression test is the honest shape of it: a core built with *no* unfocused
appearance, asserting the fallback holds and survives the reload that reads it
back. It failed first for the wrong reason - the suite's fixture passes the
settings object as the appearance, so the crashing case needed modelling
explicitly.

WT suites: terminalCore 54/54, unitSettingsModel 159/159, unitControl 61/61,
terminalApp 51/51. smoke-harness 9/9.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BgDGqEqRBB8L5Ueoq1uuxy
