+    // A SearchResults::TotalMatches meaning "nothing new to say - leave the
+    // status where it is".
+    //
+    // A negative total already means "searching", and SearchBoxControl renders
+    // it as that word. For an engine that answers a search on its own thread
+    // there is a moment on every keystroke where nothing is known yet, and
+    // saying "Searching..." for that moment reads as the status box glitching
+    // rather than as progress - it is gone before it can be read. Saying zero
+    // instead would claim there are no matches for a search that has not run.
+    //
+    // So this is the third answer: do not touch the status. During typing that
+    // leaves the previous count up until the real one arrives; on the very
+    // first search of a session it leaves the box blank, which is what it
+    // already was.
+    static constexpr int32_t SearchStatusUnchanged{ (std::numeric_limits<int32_t>::min)() };
